<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Scheme
   LastUpgradeVersion = "2700"
   version = "1.7">
   <BuildAction
      parallelizeBuildables = "YES"
      buildImplicitDependencies = "YES"
      buildArchitectures = "Automatic">
      <BuildActionEntries>
         <BuildActionEntry
            buildForTesting = "YES"
            buildForRunning = "YES"
            buildForProfiling = "YES"
            buildForArchiving = "YES"
            buildForAnalyzing = "YES">
            <BuildableReference
               BuildableIdentifier = "primary"
               BlueprintIdentifier = "DF8513BC3027B5C400F0D2D5"
               BuildableName = "Hearth.app"
               BlueprintName = "Hearth Vision"
               ReferencedContainer = "container:Hearth.xcodeproj">
            </BuildableReference>
         </BuildActionEntry>
      </BuildActionEntries>
   </BuildAction>
   <TestAction
      buildConfiguration = "Debug"
      selectedDebuggerIdentifier = "Xcode.DebuggerFoundation.Debugger.LLDB"
      selectedLauncherIdentifier = "Xcode.DebuggerFoundation.Launcher.LLDB"
      shouldUseLaunchSchemeArgsEnv = "YES"
      shouldAutocreateTestPlan = "YES">
   </TestAction>
   <!--
      THE DEBUGGER IS OFF FOR RUN ON THIS SCHEME, deliberately, and this is the
      whole of the fix rather than half of it.

      Empty selectedDebuggerIdentifier + the PosixSpawn launcher is Edit Scheme
      -> Run -> Info -> "Debug executable" unchecked. Xcode builds, installs and
      launches; LLDB never attaches.

      Why nothing less works. The checkers below inject through
      DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES, and on a visionOS device the injected dylib's load
      NOTIFICATION TO LLDB is where launch wedges -- the main thread hangs in
      dyld before main(), in loadInsertedLibraries -> registerInsertedLibrary ->
      notifyDebuggerLoad -> triggerNotifications. Disabling the checkers removes
      the dylibs but not the notify path itself, and the observed symptom with
      them off was still an infinite "Configuring Debugger Actions" that only
      cleared by killing the app and launching it from the Home View. The
      resolution recorded in /Users/jones/Valinor/tasks/visionos-crash-debug.md
      is exactly this: run without the debugger, and the app launches in about a
      second.

      The checkers stay disabled anyway, because they are what re-arms the trap
      the moment anyone ticks "Debug executable" back on to chase something.

      GPU validation and frame capture are off for the same reason and are newer
      than the rest of this comment: the target links Metal as of the face
      kernel, and frame capture AUTO-ENABLES for a Metal binary under the
      debugger. That is another launch-time layer on the one path that has
      already proven fragile here.

      WHAT THIS COSTS. No breakpoints, and `print` no longer reaches Xcode's
      console -- stdout is not the unified log. Everything worth reading on
      device therefore goes through os.Logger, which Console.app and
      `xcrun devicectl device console` both show with the debugger detached.
      To debug for real, tick "Debug executable" on and expect the first launch
      to be slow while LLDB builds its symbol cache.

      The iOS scheme keeps its debugger and both checkers. They are genuinely
      useful there, and the failure is specific to launching on a visionOS
      device.
   -->
   <LaunchAction
      buildConfiguration = "Debug"
      selectedDebuggerIdentifier = ""
      selectedLauncherIdentifier = "Xcode.IDEFoundation.Launcher.PosixSpawn"
      launchStyle = "0"
      useCustomWorkingDirectory = "NO"
      ignoresPersistentStateOnLaunch = "NO"
      debugDocumentVersioning = "YES"
      debugServiceExtension = "internal"
      allowLocationSimulation = "YES"
      disableMainThreadChecker = "YES"
      disablePerformanceAntipatternChecker = "YES"
      enableGPUValidationMode = "1"
      enableGPUFrameCaptureMode = "3">
      <BuildableProductRunnable
         runnableDebuggingMode = "0">
         <BuildableReference
            BuildableIdentifier = "primary"
            BlueprintIdentifier = "DF8513BC3027B5C400F0D2D5"
            BuildableName = "Hearth.app"
            BlueprintName = "Hearth Vision"
            ReferencedContainer = "container:Hearth.xcodeproj">
         </BuildableReference>
      </BuildableProductRunnable>
   </LaunchAction>
   <ProfileAction
      buildConfiguration = "Release"
      shouldUseLaunchSchemeArgsEnv = "YES"
      savedToolIdentifier = ""
      useCustomWorkingDirectory = "NO"
      debugDocumentVersioning = "YES">
      <BuildableProductRunnable
         runnableDebuggingMode = "0">
         <BuildableReference
            BuildableIdentifier = "primary"
            BlueprintIdentifier = "DF8513BC3027B5C400F0D2D5"
            BuildableName = "Hearth.app"
            BlueprintName = "Hearth Vision"
            ReferencedContainer = "container:Hearth.xcodeproj">
         </BuildableReference>
      </BuildableProductRunnable>
   </ProfileAction>
   <AnalyzeAction
      buildConfiguration = "Debug">
   </AnalyzeAction>
   <ArchiveAction
      buildConfiguration = "Release"
      revealArchiveInOrganizer = "YES">
   </ArchiveAction>
</Scheme>
